<title>FRANCE: Tennis-French Open men's singles results.</title>
<headline>Tennis-French Open men's singles results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Men's singles results on the second day of the French Open tennis tournament on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding</p>
<p>First round:</p>
<p>Patrik Fredriksson (Sweden) v Frederic Fontang (France) 3-6 7-6 (8-6) 0-6 6-4 bad light stopped play</p>
<p>Roberto Carretero (Spain) beat Emilio Alvarez (Spain) 5-7 7-6 (7-3) 6-3 7-5</p>
<p>Patrick Rafter (Australia) beat Andrea Gaudenzi (Italy) 3-6 7-6 (7-3) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Mark Woodforde (Australia) beat Javier Sanchez (Spain) 5-7 7-6 (8-6) 6-7 (10-12) 6-4 8-6</p>
<p>13-Wayne Ferreira (South Africa) beat Mikael Tillstrom (Sweden) 6-7 (1-7) 7-6 (7-3) 6-7 (2-7) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Petr Korda (Czech Republic) beat Jordi Burillo (Spain)  6-4 6-0 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>6-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Scott Draper (Australia) 7-6 (7-3) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Magnus Gustafsson (Sweden) beat 4-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia) 4-6 6-3 7-6 (7-3) 6-3</p>
<p>2-Michael Chang (U.S.) beat Rodolphe Gilbert (France) 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>6-2 Carlos Costa (Spain) beat Doug Flach (U.S.) 6-4 6-0 6-1</p>
<p>11-Albert Costa (Spain) beat Adrian Voinea (Romania) 6-4 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Galo Blanco (Spain) beat Neville Godwin (South Africa) 6-3 6-2 1-6 7-5</p>
<p>Andrei Pavel (Romania) beat Alex O'Brien (U.S.) 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>6-0</p>
<p>10-Felix Mantilla (Spain) beat Richard Fromberg (Australia) 6-3 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Byron Black (Zimbabwe) beat Franco Squillari (Argentina) 1-6 6-3 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>16-Sergi Bruguera (Spain) beat Johan Van Herck (Belgium) 6-3 0-6 6-2 6-0</p>
<p>Jozsef Krocsko (Hungary) beat Jan Kroslak (Slovakia) 7-5 6-3 4-6 7-6 (7-5)</p>
<p>Dennis Van Scheppingen (Netherlands) beat Paul Haarhuis(Netherlands) 6-2 6-4 5-7 6-4</p>
<p>Bohdan Ulihrach (Czech Republic) beat Nicolas Kiefer (Germany) 6-3 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Jerome Golmard (France) beat Arnaud Clement (France) 6-1 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Sandon Stolle (Australia) beat Renzo Furlan (Italy) 7-5 6-1 4-6 6-3</p>
<p>Stephane Simian (France) beat Gilbert Schaller (Austria) 2-6 6-4 4-6 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Arnaud Boetsch (France) beat Karol Kucera (Slovakia) 6-1 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Olivier Delaitre (France) beat 14-Tim Henman (Britain) 6-2 2-6 1-6 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Alexander Volkov (Russia) beat Daniel Nestor (Canada) 6-1 6-1 3-6 6-2</p>
<p>Marcos Ondruska (South Africa) beat Miguel Pastura (Argentina) 7-6 (7-3) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Magnus Larsson (Sweden) beat Jim Courier (U.S.) 6-1 6-2 4-6 1-6 6-4</p>
<p>7-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Wayne Black (Zimbabwe) 6-4 5-7 4-6 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>9-Carlos Moya (Spain) beat Alberto Martin (Spain) 6-3 6-7 (3-7) 5-7 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Dick Norman (Belgium) beat Sargis Sargsian (Armenia) 6-2 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Mark Philippoussis (Australia) beat Nicklas Kulti (Sweden) 6-2 4-6 3-6 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Todd Woodbridge (Australia) beat Kenneth Carlsen (Denmark) 7-6 (8-6) 4-6 6-4 6-0</p>
<p>Chris Woodruff (U.S.) beat Daniel Vacek (Czech Republic) 6-4 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Nicolas Lapentti (Ecuador) beat Frederik Fetterlein (Denmark) 6-4 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>Hicham Arazi (Morocco) beat Hendrik Dreekmann (Germany) 6-3 6-4 6-2</p>
